@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title cursor paradigm — policy-gated autonomous loop (layered enforcement)

actor "Developer" as DEV

node "cursor container" as CTR <<host>> {
  component "defs/cursor/entrypoint.sh" as EP <<app>>
  component "cursor-agent --force" as CLI <<app>>

  frame "Layer 1 — in-process policy" as L1 <<host>> {
    component "permissions.deny\ncli-config.json" as DENY <<error>>
    component "hooks.json\nallow / deny / ask on tool events" as HOOKS <<error>>
    component "subagents with native readonly" as RO <<app>>
  }

  database "/app — repo" as WS <<db>>
}

node "Layer 2 — container + egress" as L2 <<host>> {
  component "hardened container\ncap-drop · no-new-privileges · pids-limit" as SBX <<app>>
  component "broker egress\n(vendor-pinned inference)" as EG <<app>>
}

cloud "api2.cursor.sh\npinned TLS" as VENDOR <<cloud>>

DEV ARROW_MAIN CLI
CLI ARROW_MAIN DENY : every tool call evaluated
DENY ARROW_ERROR CLI : errorLabel(deny wins over --force)
CLI ARROW_MAIN HOOKS
HOOKS ARROW_ERROR CLI : errorLabel(root-owned — out-ranks the agent)
CLI ARROW_MAIN WS
CTR ARROW_MAIN SBX
SBX ARROW_CLOUD VENDOR : via EG

note right of L1
  **Enforcement is layered, and ""--force"" only removes
  the interactive prompt.** ""permissions.deny"" entries are
  hard stops; the enterprise hook layer is root-owned at
  ""/etc/cursor/hooks.json"" — highest precedence
  (enterprise > team > project > user), so the sandboxed
  agent can neither edit nor out-rank it.

  The harness never trusts prompt-level compliance where
  a structural control exists.
end note

note bottom of L2
  Cursor's own OS sandbox (Landlock/seccomp) is disabled
  inside the container — Docker is the boundary.
end note

note bottom of VENDOR
  **Vendor-pinned inference.** No custom base URL, so
  ""--local-model"" is rejected. Its TLS is not
  MITM-brokerable either: firewall/proxy hand the agent a
  sentinel it cannot use, so cursor defaults to **broker**
  mode, which forwards the real ""CURSOR_API_KEY"".
  The provider pin maps that key to "".cursor.sh"" /
  "".cursor.com"".
end note

note bottom of EP
  Seeds user-level config into ""${CURSOR_CONFIG_DIR:-$HOME/.cursor}""
  from baked defaults, never mutating the mounted
  workspace; detects a proxied environment and sets
  ""useHttp1ForAgent"" (agent traffic is HTTP/2 streaming by
  default, which the proxy hop cannot carry).
end note
@enduml
